---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SignupForm from '../components/SignupForm.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Tingaroo: Scratch and STEM projects for curious kids"
  description="Step-by-step Scratch and STEM projects for grades 3 to 8, with tutorials, worksheets and lesson plans for parents and teachers."
  ogDescription="Step-by-step Scratch projects for grades 3 to 8, with the guides, worksheets and lesson plans parents and teachers need to run them."
>
  <section class="container hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-accent">Scratch and STEM projects for curious kids</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Build it. Code it. Hop to the next one.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Step-by-step Scratch projects for grades 3 to 8, with the guides, worksheets and lesson plans parents and teachers need to run them.</p>

      <SignupForm id="hero" label="Get a free project tutorial by email" buttonLabel="Send me the tutorial" />
    </div>

    <div class="hero-art">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 480 360" width="100%" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="20" y="-28" width="96" height="260" rx="28" fill="#2b2d6e"/>
        <rect x="132" y="104" width="160" height="200" rx="28" fill="#ff7a1a"/>
        <rect x="308" y="-28" width="128" height="188" rx="28" fill="#16b8a6"/>
        <rect x="308" y="184" width="128" height="120" rx="28" fill="#ffc93c"/>
        <path d="M20 312 A84 84 0 0 1 188 312" fill="none" stroke="#fff8ec" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M188 312 A56 56 0 0 1 300 312" fill="none" stroke="#fff8ec" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M300 312 A36 36 0 0 1 372 312" fill="none" stroke="#fff8ec" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M372 312 A20 20 0 0 1 412 312" fill="none" stroke="#fff8ec" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="grades" class="band-white" aria-labelledby="grades-title">
    <div class="container section">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="grades-title">Projects for every step</h2>
        <p>Every project is labeled with a grade band, an age range and a time, so you can pick the right one in seconds.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-row">
        <article class="grade-card">
          <p class="tag tag-teal">Grades 3 to 4 · Ages 8 to 9</p>
          <h3>Starter</h3>
          <p class="muted">Simple games like catching stars and dodging a ghost. Short steps, big pictures, and a helper page for the grown-up nearby.</p>
          <p class="grade-tool">Made in Scratch</p>
        </article>
        <article class="grade-card">
          <p class="tag tag-orange">Grades 5 to 6 · Ages 10 to 11</p>
          <h3>Builder</h3>
          <p class="muted">Physics games with real gravity and bounce: a slingshot, a tower of boxes, a ball that must stay in the air.</p>
          <p class="grade-tool">Made in TurboWarp</p>
        </article>
        <article class="grade-card">
          <p class="tag tag-yellow">Grades 7 to 8 · Ages 12 to 13</p>
          <h3>Maker</h3>
          <p class="muted">The same games with level-up challenges: change the physics, add a score and a timer, build a second level.</p>
          <p class="grade-tool">Made in TurboWarp</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="inside" class="container section" aria-labelledby="inside-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="inside-title">What is inside every project</h2>
      <p>Everything arrives together, so nobody has to piece a lesson together the night before.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-grid">
      <li class="feature"><h3>Step-by-step tutorial</h3><p>Every step with the exact blocks to drag, shown as pictures.</p></li>
      <li class="feature"><h3>Finished project file</h3><p>Open it to see the goal, or to check a stuck student's work.</p></li>
      <li class="feature"><h3>Parent helper page</h3><p>Time, age, what you need, and what to say when a child gets stuck.</p></li>
      <li class="feature"><h3>Lesson plan</h3><p>Goals, timing, a warm-up, the main activity and a wrap-up.</p></li>
      <li class="feature"><h3>Worksheet and challenge cards</h3><p>Prompts for every student, plus extras for fast finishers.</p></li>
      <li class="feature"><h3>Rubric and answer key</h3><p>Grade a project by checking what it must contain.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="container audience-row">
    <section id="teachers" class="audience-card audience-navy" aria-labelledby="teachers-title">
      <h2 id="teachers-title">For teachers</h2>
      <p>Ready to teach with little prep, even if you have never taught coding. Each pack gives you the plan, the student pages and a way to assess the work.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Timed lesson plans for 45 to 60 minute classes</li>
        <li>Rubrics, answer keys and student worksheets</li>
        <li>Standards alignment for each project</li>
        <li>Projects that run on ordinary classroom computers</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="parents" class="audience-card audience-yellow" aria-labelledby="parents-title">
      <h2 id="parents-title">For parents and homeschoolers</h2>
      <p>Screen time that makes something. Your child builds a real game, and you do not need to know how to code to help.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A helper page with time, age and materials</li>
        <li>Prompts for what to say when they are stuck</li>
        <li>Weekend-sized projects, 30 to 60 minutes</li>
        <li>A finished example to check against</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section id="signup" class="band-orange" aria-labelledby="signup-title">
    <div class="container section signup-split">
      <div class="signup-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free tutorial · Grades 5 to 8 · 45 to 60 minutes</p>
        <h2 id="signup-title">Build a Slingshot Physics Game</h2>
        <p class="lead-dark">Launch a bird across the screen and knock down a tower. Ten steps, every block pictured, and the finished project file to open and play.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="signup-panel">
        <SignupForm
          id="foot"
          label="Where should we send it?"
          buttonLabel="Send me the free tutorial"
          layout="stacked"
          buttonStyle="navy"
          largeLabel
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="container container-narrow section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <h2 id="faq-title">Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What is Scratch?</h3>
        <p>A free coding language where kids snap blocks together to make games and animations. There is no typing of code.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do we need to buy any software?</h3>
        <p>No. Scratch and TurboWarp are free and run in a web browser. The physics games use the Physics extension in TurboWarp.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Which ages are the projects for?</h3>
        <p>Grades 3 to 8, about ages 8 to 13. Every project shows its grade band and how long it takes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is Tingaroo part of Scratch?</h3>
        <p>No. Tingaroo is independent and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Scratch Team, MIT or TurboWarp.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Who makes Tingaroo?</h3>
        <p>Basheer, a maker-educator who teaches kids to build with code and electronics. Find more of his work at <a href="https://www.basheer.diy">basheer.diy</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
